<Base
  title="About — Jeff Salleh"
  description="Senior Director at Oracle Cloud Infrastructure — and, to his knowledge, the only Asian leader who owns and runs a cloud service at Oracle. Youth advocate and community builder based in Singapore."
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="about-head">
      <div>
        <div class="post-card__meta">
          <span class="post-date">// about</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Hi, I'm Jeff.</h1>
        <p class="about-head__desc">
          Senior Director at Oracle Cloud Infrastructure — and, to my knowledge, the
          only Asian leader who owns and runs a cloud service at Oracle. Two decades in,
          still close to the code.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-head__photo">
        <img src="/images/jeff-salleh.jpg" alt="Jeff Salleh" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="post-body">
      <p>
        My career began far from home. Fresh out of Monash, I spent six months with a
        startup in Australia before deciding to return to Singapore as a wireless
        application researcher at <strong>A*STAR</strong> — the start of a lasting
        fascination with how software reaches people at scale. That path led me to
        <strong>Oracle</strong>, where I spent about a year with the wireless server team
        at headquarters in Redwood Shores before returning to Singapore to join the
        <strong>Asia R&amp;D Center</strong>, where I spent many of my most formative
        years — helping develop a number of products (a few are on my
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jeff-salleh/">LinkedIn</a>) and, the part I
        enjoyed most, driving the DevOps transformation across APAC.
      </p>

      <p>
        Today I lead within the <strong>Java Platform Group</strong> — the organisation
        that is the custodian of the Java programming language and the home of the Oracle
        Java platform. It's a rare privilege on two counts. I own and run a cloud service
        end to end — still, as far as I know, the only Asian leader at Oracle to do so.
        And I work shoulder to shoulder with some of the most capable engineers in the
        Java world, alongside my SVP, Georges Saab, who shapes how Java will continue to
        influence the enterprise for years to come. Helping steer a technology that
        quietly powers much of the modern world is not something I take lightly.
      </p>

      <p>
        Through all of it, one lesson keeps proving true: the technical work and the
        people work aren't really separate — the best engineering happens when a team
        feels trusted enough to learn out loud.
      </p>

      <h2>Youth, community, and giving back</h2>
      <p>
        Championing the next generation is close to my heart. I lead the Professional
        Network for Technology at <strong>Yayasan MENDAKI</strong>, working to help the
        Malay/Muslim community in Singapore not just find a place in tech but genuinely
        thrive in it. Over the years I've served on the <strong>National Youth Council</strong>,
        the board of Yayasan Mendaki, and as President of MendakiClub. I also founded
        <a href="https://www.voiddeck.sg">Voiddeck Ventures</a>, where we build cloud
        technology for non-profits and give young engineers real projects to learn on
        while giving back to the community.
      </p>

      <h2>What I believe</h2>
      <p>
        I care deeply about fairness, curiosity, and lifelong learning. Lately I've been
        spending a lot of time thinking about <strong>AI ethics and governance</strong> —
        how we build technology that reflects good values, not just good metrics. A line
        that has stayed with me for years — <em>"My Lord, increase me in knowledge"</em> —
        is more or less how I try to approach my work, my teams, and this blog. I studied
        Network Computing at Monash and later went through Stanford GSB's LEAD program,
        but honestly, most of what matters I've learned by building alongside good people.
      </p>

      <h2>What I write about</h2>
      <p>
        Engineering leadership, cloud and the Java platform, growing teams, AI governance,
        and the place where technology, community, and values meet. Sometimes in English,
        occasionally with a Malay proverb thrown in.
      </p>

      <h2>Say hello</h2>
      <p>
        Whether you're a peer, a student, or just starting to find your way in tech —
        especially if you're a young technologist looking for a way in — I'd genuinely
        like to hear from you. Reach me at
        <a href="mailto:jeff@voiddeck.sg">jeff@voiddeck.sg</a>
        or connect on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jeff-salleh/">LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
